{"completed": true, "response": "<escape>{\n  \"report_supported\": \"partly\",\n  \"judge_supported\": \"partly\",\n  \"report_quotes\": [\n    \"NOTE: This preprint reports new research that has not been certified by peer review and should not be used to guide clinical practice.\",\n    \"Four participants exhibited frequent episodes of freezing of gait, predominantly whilst turning.\",\n    \"We exploited this platform in 18 patients with Parkinson’s disease, which allowed us to demonstrate that the subthalamic nucleus encodes the initiation, termination, and vigor of leg muscle activation.\",\n    \"20 patients with Parkinson’s disease were recruited for the study.\",\n    \"Overall, 17 patients were retained for analyses on the neurorobotic platform and 12 for gait experiments.\"\n  ],\n  \"judge_quotes\": [\n    \"NOTE: This preprint reports new research that has not been certified by peer review and should not be used to guide clinical practice.\",\n    \"We exploited this platform in 18 patients with Parkinson’s disease, which allowed us to demonstrate that the subthalamic nucleus encodes the initiation, termination, and vigor of leg muscle activation.\",\n    \"20 patients with Parkinson’s disease were recruited for the study.\",\n    \"Overall, 17 patients were retained for analyses on the neurorobotic platform and 12 for gait experiments.\",\n    \"Four participants exhibited frequent episodes of freezing of gait, predominantly whilst turning.\"\n  ],\n  \"why\": \"两方的说法均有部分依据。第一，附件全文明确标注为medRxiv预印本，并明确声明尚未经过同行评审，因此报告对附件所代表版本的预印本属性判断有直接依据。仅凭这份全文，无法证实指控者所说的PMID对应Science Translational Medicine正式发表版本；全文也没有提供该期刊的发表信息。第二，FOG相关分析确实涉及4名患者，全文明确写道有4名参与者出现频繁的冻结步态事件。但是，样本量需要区分不同统计口径：摘要和结果部分报告18名患者；Methods明确写明实际招募20名患者，其中17名纳入神经机器人平台分析、12名纳入步态实验分析；FOG部分则涉及4名患者。因此，指控者关于4人属于FOG相关分析子集的判断有依据，但将18人直接称为整个研究的总招募队列并不严谨，因为Methods明确记载招募人数为20人。报告将4人作为相关分析样本有依据，但如果没有说明其属于FOG子集，也没有交代更大的研究队列及不同分析的人数，就缺少重要的样本范围限定。综上，报告的说法为partly，指控者的说法也为partly。\"\n}</escape>", "metadata": {"session_handle": "6d82f1e8-df24-4249-bae8-e5363897f4f4", "session_revision": 0, "session_ttl_max_hours": 6, "job_directory": "D:\\musicclaude\\gpt2agent-safechain\\runs\\gpt4\\pro-bridge-20261113T125138066494Z", "elapsed_seconds": 73.969, "completed_utc": "2026-11-13T12:52:52.045356+00:00", "model": "gpt-6-thinking", "thinking_effort": "max", "temporary": true, "unpersonalized": true, "generation_policy_verified": true, "request_policy": {"model": "gpt-6-thinking", "thinking_effort": "max", "history_and_training_disabled": true, "temporary_chat_requests_personalization": false, "is_do_not_remember": false, "continuation": false, "unpersonalized_inherited_verified": false, "body_sha256": "85029fc4a81e134cbd4f173af4da7bf6f441a4626444e246140f703c2cdb5382", "attachment_count": 1}, "stream_completion": {"sse_done": true, "message_completed": true, "independent_terminal_verified": true}, "profile": "Nozomi Kasaki / gpt4", "account_sha256": "bbd4fd636d4b6714d2b42b89e341bdb5bbe7c34f7d141aec76b444be8343fe54", "transport": "probridge-pure-http", "resume_requests": 0, "topic_connections": 0, "browser_started": false, "Docker_used": false, "automatic_retry": false, "initializer_pss_limit_mib": "not_applicable_no_browser", "attachment_count": 1, "code_sha256": {"tools\\chatgpt_web\\gpt3_cli.py": "96a4cdb6cd5d982f4d1de5b6ba8fae0cf23ee44aa3e41d7fdf6968e3fb590e48", "tools\\chatgpt_web\\gpt3_sessions.py": "83a3ed4ae1efa9f1a2b8ee3f144cc0dc9f668f995a33cc4222308cb3fa31f683", "tools\\chatgpt_web\\gpt3_attachments.py": "eedfa23885000025700f6306b1d1f4582896a7370734be506c156dee532fd7d7"}}, "screenshot_evidence": {"complete": true, "kind": "offline_actual_HTTP_response", "directory": "D:\\musicclaude\\gpt2agent-safechain\\runs\\gpt4\\pro-bridge-20261113T125138066494Z", "files": ["proof-offline.png"], "sha256": {"proof-offline.png": "51046786167be2e06b6d277fad168e785317e2a882e2d2951ff8c85572d87388"}}}
